WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.580
Twin Eagle, engage in the most challenging shoot-em-up action-packed game yet for the Nintendo Entertainment System.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:29.060
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.020
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.020
And today we will be taking revenge on Joe's brother.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.040
No, that's the hidden subtitle of Twin Eagle.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.980
And though Joe is not here and he does have a brother,

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:50.780
you know, I think like for folks that aren't familiar with the like box art of the game,

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.100
the revenge of Joe's brother's thing is very well hidden.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.240
And then the menu makes it seem like that was always the title.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.120
But it's just kind of a hidden subtitle in the game.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.280
And shouldn't it be a then?

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.440
Yeah, it should. Not revenge?

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:09.280
It's really funny because it also like not only is it grammatically incorrect,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.880
but it also has this really goofy font.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.580
It makes it look like it was added like way later for no reason.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.560
It's great.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.240
I love it. It put me in a good mood.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:24.560
And also, you know, I can't help but notice that there's only one eagle on the box art.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.000
And I'm not talking about the helicopters.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.580
There's actually they put it. They put a bald eagle on the box art at that point.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.600
If you're going to if you're going to go that route, you might as well put two right.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.500
I mean calling your game twin eagle.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:44.940
Sure. But like, does a twin stop being a twin if if his if the brother and or sister is not around?

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.240
I think you're you're a twin.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.980
That eagle is still a twin, even though its sibling isn't there.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.220
You know, just saying.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:55.520
Okay, sure.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:07.180
You know, and I know that like the helicopter, whatever is called the twin eagle or whatever, you know, we always I don't seem to care when these vehicles are named after real life things.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.280
But I don't think so.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.840
I think it's just talking about that eagle that you don't see any time after this.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:17.420
Got it. Okay. No, that that could be, too, because the box art, the subtitle, it's all very confusing.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.240
But but there is a game inside of there, and it is a vertical helicopter shmup.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.520
Certainly not our first go around with helicopter shoot them ups.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.760
And I don't know if you want to, like, comment on that at all.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.400
Sean, I wasn't expecting so many helicopter shmups on the system.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.760
No, I seem to be hot in the 80s.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:47.340
I'd say that is one of like if anybody were to pose the question, like in 2030, when we finally played all these games, like what did you find most interesting?

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:55.320
What's surprising about all these games at NostalgiaCon 2031 or whatever?

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:03.040
It would be how many how many helicopter shmups there were at full stop.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.600
But we're not going to beef on helicopters or anything.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:06.920
That's what they've decided on.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.440
I've seen other shmups decide on other weird things, too.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.900
We had one where you were caveman.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:14.660
So I guess this is, you know, more true to anything.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.080
You are.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.080
You're not playing as Joe.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.100
You're not playing as his buddy.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.240
I don't think your brother.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.220
Yeah, the brother or whatever.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:26.360
Yeah, sorry. His buddy.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:37.240
But you are the, you know, the lone helicopter that's going to once again take down an entire army because they killed Joe's brother.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.600
Now, that seems like a lot, you know, I don't know.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:48.180
Usually it's that the army is also simultaneously like taking over the world or, you know, it's a historical fight kind of thing.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.720
This seems like a lot for just one death.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:59.500
I mean, if you're an acquaintance of of Joe's brother, like you would lay yourself on the line to rescue and or avenge him.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.380
That's from as far as I can tell.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.400
Can you be sure that all these guys were responsible for killing Joe's brother?

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:11.720
I mean, now you're getting into, you know, who's responsible for anything, really.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.780
I mean, aren't we all just, you know, slaves to our circumstances?

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:20.500
You know how like there's an alternate universe for everything?

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:35.840
Yeah. Well, this game is simultaneously creating all different kinds of spinoffs of all of the avenging brothers that we have killed in this game because their brothers will surely answer the call to take down the army that you are playing as.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:42.080
Yeah. I mean, you know, eye for an eye and then everybody's got one eye.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.960
And everybody's got a brother.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.300
Yeah, I would.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:46.500
I would assume so.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:52.760
Anyway, you know, why do you think we've been harping on this specific element of the game for so long, Mike?

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:58.080
Well, because we played a lot of shmups and we're kind of running out of things to talk about and we have many more to go.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.420
So I would like to talk about the game if that's okay with everybody for a minute.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.980
The helicopter itself.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:10.680
Okay. There are a couple of noticeable changes here that I like.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:17.020
The things that I noticed that I was like, wow, that's actually an interesting design decision, whether they intended it or not.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:24.600
The first being that there is no enemy collision between your helicopter and any of the enemies on screen.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:40.580
Finally, a game that gets that like just because it's a top down 2D game doesn't mean that everybody's on the same Z axis as each other that it's very possible that the planes are above you and the tanks are below you.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:51.640
In fact, any kind of collision with a tank and a helicopter makes me question the sanity of the helicopter pilot that was flying that low that he collided into the tank.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.920
It really would be our fault if that were to happen.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.660
But I think that that's that's totally valid.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:02.800
Like that's that's something that's that that should be the case.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:13.160
But then you also have to wonder, like, okay, so that just means that every bullet that's fired is just like auto locking ground air air to ground.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:17.920
And I get the you know that that that's something I'm willing to like to accept.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.360
Yeah. Well, how do you think they took down Joe's brother?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.780
That's true. I mean, but Joe's brother that auto locking technology.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.600
Yeah. I mean, who knew if Joe's brother was in a helicopter?

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.020
He may have just been on the ground like a goofball.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.380
We don't know how he died.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.820
Now, movement, though, as the helicopter.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:44.100
Yes, there is a power up to become faster, which ultimately just makes the helicopter even more twitchy in terms of its responsiveness.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:47.880
But I don't feel like I'm controlling a helicopter at all here.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:07:00.380
It's really hard to circle around with the with the D-pad here, which is interesting, given the fact that it is a helicopter and would presumably be best at turning around full stop and stuff like that.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.320
But here we have a game that.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:09.580
You know, to be fair, the enemies are just as slow outside of the hyper speed parts of the game.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.880
So movement in general is just defined this way.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:16.080
I just don't know if I like my shmups to be slower paced.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:23.240
This is more so like when you start to sell your product on like what you're controlling.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:27.460
Like, OK, yeah, you've played shmup before, but have you played shmup as helicopter?

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.680
I want I want the helicopter to feel differently.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:35.860
And unfortunately, like they could have changed the sprite to literally anything.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.920
And it would have played like any other vertically scrolling shooter.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:51.220
Like I think maybe if they added some like deceleration or acceleration changes to just the way it controlled, I could buy it that like, OK, it makes sense.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:55.320
This is a helicopter and not like some slow moving plane or whatever.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.640
So, yeah, I agree that it felt wrong.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:10.440
And another plus for it, though, the coloring of the enemy bullets for maybe the first time in a shmup, like they really want you to.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:18.100
It's almost like remember in the 90s when the hockey pucks and the NHL got like they got like a highlighter color around them.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.200
Yeah, this way you could keep your eyes on it.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.660
It's like, I don't know if that needed it.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:30.680
But certainly certain shmups did need it because there's so many bullets on screen that sometimes it gets a little hard to keep track of those little white pixels.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:36.080
Here they are nice red and yellow flickering balls.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.640
You know, they're not they're not trying to look like bullets at all.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:42.160
And I feel like they those read really well on the screen.

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:43.320
I agree. You're right.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:46.860
There are some nice accessibility things going on here.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.100
And I appreciate that.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.620
Accessibility, I think, is the is the best point about this game, too.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.660
Visually, it's not doing anything we haven't seen before.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.260
Level design, it definitely isn't doing anything we've seen before.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:10.880
It's a lot of just constantly repeating enemies and uninteractable environments and stuff like that that just change level to level as you move across a map.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:17.940
But in terms of controls, I think that's where this game shines over a lot of shmups that we've played.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:25.620
Well, real quick, I just want to go back to the visual design and then I'm going to come back to this controls thing.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:34.480
One thing that I will say that I think that this game sort of stands above is specifically the way that they that they treat water.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.640
Water looks cool.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:38.440
And it's not just the same repeating pattern over and over.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:44.800
There's some areas that glisten in the sunlight and some areas that, you know, look just sort of, you know, there.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:48.720
But I appreciate that water was at least interesting to look at.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:52.820
Now, back to your your controls.

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:55.620
How? I actually didn't catch this.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:58.920
It felt kind of how everything else feels to me.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:00.920
Okay. So, yeah, it is.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.620
It is just firing bullets and dropping bombs.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.100
We've seen all that before.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:10.360
And, you know, with only two buttons on an NES, that's mostly what you're going to run into in any shmup.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:16.760
The bombs have an interesting quirk, though, that I really like from a from a shmup strategy point of view.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:24.140
And that is that on top of destroying every single enemy on screen is if you've dropped some kind of nuke and your helicopters nuke proof.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:33.980
It also destroys every enemy bullet on screen, which is a really good way of getting like a last second dodge in like an inescapable moment.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.120
You can just throw the bomb instead.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.820
And we haven't seen that in any game where you're actually erasing firepower.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:43.120
So, you know, that I really appreciated.

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:44.460
I don't know.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.500
I mean, erasing firepower.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:53.240
I feel like the last shmup that we played had a similar had a similar quirk to its bombs.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.700
But I might be I might be misremembering it.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:58.020
I will take your word for it.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.680
Since I can't speak to the specific game.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:05.900
And then the power ups, you know, they are nothing to write home about.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:09.520
And none of them are entirely, you know, like more useful than the other.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:13.740
Some have a little bit of a larger spray, but nothing nothing terrific.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:17.220
Other ones let you shoot backwards, but not strong enough.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.700
They'll have like their trade off.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.520
So there's nothing like you don't feel powerful at any given stage.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:28.800
But what I like about it is, you know, you shoot at the power up to rotate through a number of different power ups.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:32.360
We've seen this even in games that we like, like Stinger and stuff like that.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:38.920
But when you shoot through them, you're collecting a new kind of power up.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:45.560
But if you collect the same power up three times, you have the chance to continue to level it up to its level three power.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:51.380
When you collect a new power up after you're like, let's say you're level three black S, right?

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:57.880
But then you suddenly collect a black P and I'm giving the color because sometimes that's all you have to go off of too.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.400
There's like multiple different S's.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:00.600
There's multiple different P's.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:08.480
So when you collect a black P after being on a level three black S, a normal shmup would reset you.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:13.600
It would bring you way back to level one now and be punished for picking up this new kind of power up.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:18.880
With this game, they keep you at level three and now you just have the best of that type.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:26.940
And the strategy is really just stay alive as long as you can because when you crash, you're reset to no power ups and base level.

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:37.460
So that I felt like was a we've seen it before another mechanic where nothing new, but the way that they did it made it more.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:44.020
Yeah, they streamlined it, but also like it makes the game a little bit easier without, you know, not making it challenging.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:46.560
Like the one hit KO is still there.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:54.260
The amount of bullets on screen can still get very high, but I didn't feel I didn't feel like this game was unfair.

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:58.880
Yeah, I'd still say it's hard, but you're right.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:06.600
Like it's not and you're still going to be punished if you lose all your power ups late in the game.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:18.320
But it's not as punishing as we're used to in this genre and all these other sort of iterations on the design of shmups.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:27.020
Like there's nothing revolutionary here, but they've made a lot of small adjustments to make it just a little bit easier on you, I'd say.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:38.420
And I'll admit that I did say at first, you know, that I might have sounded like I was talking about being the helicopter, like the controls of a helicopter being the selling point of the game.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:41.880
These are more game design decisions than anything else.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:45.800
The actual helicopter gameplay is is rather boring.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.720
And so are the power ups that come with it.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:52.980
It's just that it happens to work as a as a cohesive element.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:14:01.880
You know, like everything seems to work in favor of making making it feel a little easier, a little stronger as you continue to progress.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.180
And yeah, it's easily wiped away.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:11.120
But at least there's some instinctual like knowledge to how to build up power in this game.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.420
It doesn't like just because it's it's not very unique in any way.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.060
At least it doesn't feel jank.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:21.900
And there's no bosses in this game at all, which is which is an interesting thing.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:29.500
Like the game has a moment where all of a sudden you just go into hyperspeed and everything just scrolls a lot faster.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:32.800
You don't move any faster, which is a strange decision.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:34.700
But all the enemies do.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:38.160
And if you can survive that, that's the end of the level.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:42.600
There is no big helicopter or big tank or anything.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.160
You know, usually that's what we see in these schmups.

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:46.800
Just like a bigger sprite of something that's already pretty intimidating.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:56.200
With weak points. We don't get that here, which makes me wonder what's up with the claim on the back of the box that this is the most challenging shoot them up action pack game yet.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:15:00.060
I get that that's ad speak, you know, like sure.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:07.820
But like we've had good challenging and we've had Nintendo hard challenging way beyond what this game is offering.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.860
I mean, what are they going to say that like, yeah, there's another one.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:12.780
No, absolutely.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:22.400
I just think that, you know, I have to address that because when we call out the back of the boxes for this games, obviously they're writing that copy and not me.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:27.520
But you have to think about if that's what they were going for is a challenging game.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:31.900
I feel like you could have sold a lot of other things about this game instead.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:37.180
Maybe avenging Joe's brother since you didn't mention it anywhere in the box.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:53.140
I think that like if they put in some cut scenes, like maybe even some flashbacks of like you hanging out with Joe's brother and then like between each level just having like what's going on with Joe's brother or like what what did he mean to you?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.380
That this could have like that could have been what they sold in the back of the box.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:01.740
And I would have had a lot more like I would I would have wanted to see what happened next.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:04.400
Like, did you go to the bar with Joe's brother?

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:07.100
Like, were you dating his sister?

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:12.460
I don't know. Like, well, how do I why do I care about Joe's brother?

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:16.800
Well, they don't give a shit about the plot anyway, Sean, because towards the end of the game.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.080
First off, there's a map.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:19.460
OK, we need to get that.

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:27.160
There is a map that it's a act like a mission map, but it just shows you how much closer you are to a castle.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:32.300
I suppose that, you know, because it's not a we're not going after a country per se.

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:43.080
We're going after the people who killed Joe's brother that where it all leads up to a castle that shows you like how many enemies you've defeated and hostages you've saved other brothers.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:46.420
You might have said all that stuff is just points and dressing.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:50.060
It's not really anything, you know, anything exciting.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.220
It doesn't make it the adventure feel grander.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:58.100
But the reason I say I don't give a shit about the plot is because then you get to the castle and it's not a boss fight.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:04.280
It's still just like enemy helicopters coming out of places while you shoot them and the castle, which does not fight back.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:05.880
That would be kind of interesting if it did.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:11.240
And then it just tells you, you know, just in plain text, white text on black.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:15.460
You've just beaten the evil monster who was sent to destroy the earth.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:20.580
What? That's like a totally different plot to a different game.

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.160
That was never set up for me.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:25.020
I OK, so I did not beat this game.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.640
This is news to me.

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:34.620
I knew that you fought like over a castle, but I did not know that's how it ended.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:38.340
And there's some inexplicable monster side story.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:41.080
Now I now I'm even more curious.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.080
Now I want that story even more.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:45.300
And who was the monster?

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:46.380
Was it the castle?

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:50.360
Like we didn't get to fight some Godzilla sized monster.

